# Keep line endings stable across operating systems.
#
# Why this file exists: Prettier enforces `endOfLine: "lf"` and ESLint reports a
# `Delete ␍` error for every CRLF line. On Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`, git
# checked files out as CRLF, producing ~3660 lint errors locally while CI
# (Linux) stayed green. The blobs committed in git are already LF — this file
# makes the Windows working tree match them.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides the local `core.autocrlf` setting for text files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.apk binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary

# Windows batch scripts require CRLF to run correctly (e.g. android/gradlew.bat).
# `-text` leaves them untouched so git never normalizes or warns about them.
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text
*.ps1 -text
